     When you press <enter> while looking at the inventory display,
you're dismissing the --More-- prompt which has paused nethack's
output.  In a menu, <enter> means that you're satisfied with
whatever selection(s) you've made, so it closes the menu.  Aside
from '>' which was previously mentioned, <space> will take you to
the next page of a menu.  It also works at --More--, so you might
want to start using it instead of <enter> there too.  Once you
figure out how to make persistent options settings :-) you should
make sure that rest_on_space is toggled off instead of on.  (Off
is the default setting inside the program, but the template options
file for Windows sets it to be on.)  If you have rest_on_space
enabled, it's inevitable that you'll eventually end up wasting a
turn and getting killed when you press <space> in advance because
you expected to be stuck at --More-- in some situation where it
failed to occur.  (When rest_on_space is off, you need to use '.'
instead of <space> to intentionally waste a turn.)


